\f0\fs24 \cf2 Look closely at this room: it\'92s the Valtellinese Stove Room\'85 surprising, isn\'92t it?\
Now, play a game: compare it with the historical photograph preserved in the museum's archive. Almost everything is in its place, identical to how the Bagatti Valsecchi brothers imagined it in the 19th century. It\'92s as if time has stopped. Of course, some details have changed. The large central rug is no longer there, and the cabinet you see in the photo has been replaced by something truly special: a piano, made by Achille Merico based on designs by the brothers themselves. A unique piece, blending music and craftsmanship, just as they liked it.\
Close your eyes for a moment. Imagine being here, sitting around the lit fireplace on a winter evening. The flames dancing, the smell of burning wood, the notes of a waltz filling the room, the warmth of the Valtellinese stove enveloping everything.\
It\'92s more than just a room: it\'92s an invitation to slow down, to rediscover the value of time, conviviality, and craftsmanship that can warm even the soul.\
And you\'85 can you see yourself sitting there, in this warm embrace of history and beauty?}